                ✔ 8-REFACTOR: net layer moved behind a transport port @done(26-08-14) (CODE ONLY —
                   NOT RE-VERIFIED IN GAME. Deep-module pass, no feature change intended.
                   New IForgeTransport with OfflineTransport / PunTransport adapters; all 11
                   sends and every authority read now go through it, so PhotonNetwork appears
                   in exactly one type. The four gate rules (IsAuthority / ShouldBroadcast /
                   ShouldRelay / targeted-send) are stated together and were checked
                   ALGEBRAICALLY equivalent to the old PhotonNetwork expressions, not just by
                   eye: ShouldBroadcast expands to (!InRoom||IsMaster) && InRoom && Count>1,
                   which collapses to the original InRoom && IsMaster && Count>1.
                   Bonus: the Awake hazard from 8-REGRESSION is now STRUCTURAL, not a rule to
                   remember — the transport starts as OfflineTransport, which references nothing
                   from Photon, so PunTransport isn't loaded until a room event fires.
                   Also: snapshot payloads now encode in ONE place (ForgeSnapshot.ToPayload /
                   TryFromPayload) instead of three hand-rolled copies in ForgeNetSync; commit
                   status text now formats in ONE place (ForgeLabels.DescribeCommit) instead of
                   two copies that had already drifted; EscalationIntensity.Current replaces a
                   4-line preamble that 5 sites each carried; config defaults now live in one
                   const per entry (the scalar cap default alone had SIX copies).
                   77 new xunit tests, 225 passing — first coverage the net layer has ever had.
                   TWO BUGS FIXED: _pendingModuleOverlay was never cleared on room leave (only
                   _pendingCursed was), so a stale overlay could survive a room change and be
                   applied to whatever unrelated object inherited the ViewID; and the
                   module-overlay decode didn't normalise empty perk slots ""→null the way the
                   commit-result decode always did.
                   ONE REAL RUNTIME DIFFERENCE, highest re-test risk: targeted late-joiner
                   sends used to receive Photon's Player object directly, and now take an actor
                   number the adapter resolves via CurrentRoom.GetPlayer(actorNumber,false).
                   If that lookup ever returns null the push SILENTLY no-ops, which would look
                   exactly like a joiner getting a clean slate → T6 is the test for it.
