                ✔ BuildBox "floats away" REGRESSED in MP @done(26-07-18) (CODE ONLY — bug is rare and
                   was NOT reproduced on demand, so this is verified by reasoning + logging, not by
                   repro. Reported: picking a box off the forge, it drifted out of the HOLDER's own
                   hands; intermittent ("does not happen often"); solo not re-checked.
                   ROOT CAUSE: CarryableObject is an ISimulatedBody — while riding a MovingSpacePlatform
                   (the ship) its real physics lives on SimulationRigidbody in a SEPARATE physics
                   scene, not on MainRigidbody. Note Rigidbody and MainRigidbody both return the same
                   field, so there is no "active body" accessor. The 26-07-14 fix wrote velocity
                   straight to MainRigidbody, so whenever platform simulation was active the
                   accumulated velocity survived on the simulation body and the box drifted anyway —
                   which is exactly why it was intermittent rather than constant. Dock() froze only
                   MainRigidbody for the same reason, leaving the sim body integrating the whole time
                   it was docked.
                   ALSO FOUND: the Velocity property's non-simulated branch is
                   `else if (!rigidBody.isKinematic)` — writing velocity to a still-kinematic body is
                   SILENTLY DROPPED. Order now is clear-kinematic THEN zero; the old code's ordering
                   may be why it appeared to work at all.
                   FIX: new SetDockedKinematic freezes/unfreezes BOTH bodies (unconditionally — the
                   IsBeingSimulated flag can flip while an item sits docked); release zeroes through
                   the Velocity/AngularVelocity properties so it hits whichever body is live (zero is
                   space-invariant: the simulated branch applies an inverse platform rotation).
                   DELIBERATELY NOT CHANGED: PlaceAtAnchor still pins the visual transform directly.
                   Driving it through co.Position/co.Rotation would be "correct by the interface", but
                   the simulated branch writes into a separate scene and the decompile is ambiguous
                   about whether it wants world or platform-local coords — feeding it the wrong space
                   would teleport the box every frame, far worse than a rare drift. Freezing the sim
                   body removes the accumulation at its source without needing to resolve that.
                   RESIDUAL RISK: sim body position may be stale on release. That would present as a
                   SNAP, not a drift — distinguishable in play, and the new log line calls it out.
                   [] VERIFY: new "[Forge] undock <name>: simulated=T/F, was=(x,y,z)" LogDebug on every
                      undock. simulated=True with a non-zero `was=` is the signature of the old bug;
                      seeing simulated=True with the box behaving = fix holding. Watch for a snap-back.
                   [] STILL UNKNOWN: does it repro in SOLO? Never checked. If it does, MP was a red
                      herring and this fix is still right (simulation is active in solo too).)
                ✔ hangar load hitch / lag spike on ship select @done(26-07-18) (CODE ONLY. PreloadAll
                   iterated every ShipLoadoutDataDef — that's every LOADOUT PRESET, not every ship —
                   and loaded the referenced prefab per preset. ~19 Destroyer presets all point at
                   MTM_Destroyer_01, so it built that ship 19 times (455-618 renderers each) and
