                   so reasoned from source rather than validated. Full write-up with citations:
                   docs/chat-bug-research.md. BOTH reported symptoms are VANILLA bugs; VoidCrewTerminus
                   is not implicated (it only consumes VoidManager's chat router) and VoidManager does
                   NOT fix them — its README claims only mouse-unlock, input history and tab-complete,
                   all postfix-only additions.
                   SYMPTOM 2 (input eaten) — FIXED: TextChatVE.GetMessage blanks the field while it
                   still holds focus with a live cursor, and HideInput only toggles CSS classes — there
                   is no Blur()/SelectNone() anywhere in the chat code. The stale selection range then
                   indexes past the end of an empty string and Unity throws
                   ArgumentOutOfRangeException in TextEditingUtilities.ReplaceSelection on EVERY later
                   keypress (Unity issue tracker confirms that behaviour; the exact stack is in our
                   captured log). Permanence comes from TextChat's "TextChatting" state, which only
                   RemoveInput() clears and which silently fails to clear when LocalPlayer.I is null.
                   FIX (Patches/ChatInputFixPatch.cs): postfix GetMessage + HideInput → SelectNone() +
                   Blur(), mirroring the game's OWN correct pattern in UIToolkitNavigationExtensions;
                   prefix OpenChat → clear a stale "TextChatting" via the game's own RemoveInput (works
                   there because OpenChat dereferences LocalPlayer.I, so it's alive by then). All
                   members via AccessTools with one-shot resolve logging — a game update that moves the
                   vanilla UI makes it inert and SAYS so rather than failing CreateAndPatchAll.
                   Config EnableChatInputFix (default on).
                   SYMPTOM 1 (chat sends nothing) — DOCUMENTED, NOT FIXED: VoipBoostrap.OnJoinedRoom
                   discards the Task from LeaveChannels() then immediately JoinChannels(); a late leave
                   tears down the channels just joined (our log shows exactly that order), leaving
                   textChannel empty so VivoxAdapter.SendTextMessage hits a silent return. A local echo
                   masks it from the sender. Not fixed: reordering async Vivox lifecycle from a Harmony
                   patch risks breaking voice chat too. Candidate upstream report.
